#: ../pwntools/docs/source/regsort.rst:6
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib.regsort` --- Register sorting"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort:1
msgid "Topographical sort"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.check_cycle:1
msgid ""
"Walk down the assignment list of a register, return the path walked if it"
" is encountered again."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.check_cycle pwnlib.regsort.regsort
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.check_cycle:4
msgid ""
"The list of register involved in the cycle. If there is no cycle, this is"
" an empty list."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.check_cycle:8 pwnlib.regsort.extract_dependencies:5
#: pwnlib.regsort.regsort:58 pwnlib.regsort.resolve_order:4
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.extract_dependencies:1
msgid ""
"Return a list of all registers which directly depend on the specified "
"register."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:1
msgid "Sorts register dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:3
msgid ""
"Given a dictionary of registers to desired register contents, return the "
"optimal order in which to set the registers to those contents."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:7
msgid ""
"The implementation assumes that it is possible to move from any register "
"to any other register."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:10
msgid "If a dependency cycle is encountered, one of the following will occur:"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:13
msgid ""
"If ``xchg`` is :const:`True`, it is assumed that dependency cyles can be "
"broken by swapping the contents of two register (a la the ``xchg`` "
"instruction on i386)."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:16
msgid ""
"If ``xchg`` is not set, but not all destination registers in ``in_out`` "
"are involved in a cycle, one of the registers outside the cycle will be "
"used as a temporary register, and then overwritten with its final value."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:20
msgid ""
"If ``xchg`` is not set, and all registers are involved in a dependency "
"cycle, the named register ``temporary`` is used as a temporary register."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:23
msgid ""
"If the dependency cycle cannot be resolved as described above, an "
"exception is raised."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:26
msgid ""
"Dictionary of desired register states. Keys are registers, values are "
"either registers or any other value."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:29
msgid ""
"List of all possible registers. Used to determine which values in "
"``in_out`` are registers, versus regular values."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:33
msgid ""
"Named register (or other sentinel value) to use as a temporary register."
"  If ``tmp`` is a named register **and** appears as a source value in "
"``in_out``, dependencies are handled appropriately.  ``tmp`` cannot be a "
"destination register in ``in_out``. If ``bool(tmp)==True``, this mode is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:40
msgid ""
"Indicates the existence of an instruction which can swap the contents of "
"two registers without use of a third register. If ``bool(xchg)==False``, "
"this mode is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:44
msgid "Randomize as much as possible about the order or registers."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:47
msgid ""
"A list of tuples of ``(src, dest)``.  Each register may appear more than "
"once, if a register is used as a temporary register, and later "
"overwritten with its final value.  If ``xchg`` is :const:`True` and it is"
" used to break a dependency cycle, then ``reg_name`` will be "
":const:`None` and ``value`` will be a tuple of the instructions to swap."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:47
msgid "A list of tuples of ``(src, dest)``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:49
msgid ""
"Each register may appear more than once, if a register is used as a "
"temporary register, and later overwritten with its final value."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:53
msgid ""
"If ``xchg`` is :const:`True` and it is used to break a dependency cycle, "
"then ``reg_name`` will be :const:`None` and ``value`` will be a tuple of "
"the instructions to swap."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:61
msgid "If order doesn't matter for any subsequence, alphabetic order is used."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.regsort:68
msgid ""
"Registers which are assigned one of their own aliases are dropped, like "
"same-name self-assignments."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.regsort.resolve_order:1
msgid "Resolve the order of all dependencies starting at a given register."
msgstr ""

